.expo/
# package-lock.json is COMMITTED. It used to be ignored, which meant EAS logged
# "No lockfile found" and resolved every dependency fresh on every build: builds
# were not reproducible, expo doctor failed on it, and a transitive update could
# break a release with no commit to blame. It is exactly how vitest 5 arrived and
# took an APK down.

# One-off patch scripts
fix_*.py
check_*.py

# Expo export output
dist/

# Scratch files
patch_jobs.py


